id: pm-context-lk82
title: Adopt sdk/query context engine and drop spawnSync shell-outs
description: "Replace the spawnSync pm list-all shell-out in index.ts with the typed in-process list action from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core. Rank filtered candidates with rankContextItems/createSdkRanker over the SDK relevance model, pack max-items requests with createSdkPacker over packContextCandidates plus a hard count ceiling, record/read context usage through SDK query APIs, and expose --explain through buildContextExplain/scoreContextItems over the emitted pack."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T11:59:46.130Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T15:08:27.515Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T12:18:15.732Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "Review findings corrected: explain now uses the exact packed focus and neighborhood membership, all emitted ledger rows are included, and SDK list preserves legacy truncation semantics."
expected_result: "The in-process SDK path preserves previous query behavior, explains only items the normal pack emits after neighborhood and budget selection, and records every visible item as served."
actual_result: "A real SDK-host integration test now proves neighborhood inclusion, max-items exclusion, explain non-mutation, and included serving rows; 78 of 78 tests pass."
notes[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T11:59:50.739Z",pi-agent,"Confirmed @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core list({full,includeBody,noTruncate,excludeTerminal:false},{pmRoot}) returns byte-identical items to spawnSync pm list-all --json --include-body (24/24 ids match, item JSON equal). Replacing readPmItems shell-out with in-process SDK call."
  "2026-07-26T12:18:01.328Z",claude,"Verified by orchestrator (claude): typecheck OK, 77/77 tests pass, build OK. Functional proof in a throwaway workspace — installed the built extension and ran 'pm context-pack --status in_progress --explain', which returned real per-signal scores from the SDK relevance model (model=default-weighted-v1; signals structural, recency, graph_proximity, claim_focus, priority_pressure, risk_pressure, deadline_pressure, knowledge_density, author_affinity). Fixed one residual typecheck error the agent did not reach: local PmItem.parent was 'string | undefined' but the SDK ListResultItem.parent is 'string | null | undefined'; widened the local type to match rather than casting."
  "2026-07-26T14:28:44.566Z",codex,"CodeRabbit review findings were reproduced and fixed. Upstream pm-cli TOON round-trip defect discovered during pm validate is tracked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/747; the package does not work around or rewrite core storage."
  "2026-07-26T14:33:47.372Z",codex,"Strict source hygiene also replaced two literal NUL bytes in context-usage.ts with the behavior-identical TypeScript unicode escape, so tooling treats the source as text."
  "2026-07-26T14:35:14.059Z",codex,"Final contract audit preserved SDK token-budget optimization while adding a deterministic post-pack count ceiling, so --max-items can never emit more items than documented. The real tracker integration proves max-items=1 emits and explains exactly one item."
  "2026-07-26T14:40:58.448Z",codex,DeepScan post-push analysis reported two unused sdk/query imports. Removed CONTEXT_RELEVANCE_SIGNAL_NAMES and PackedContextCandidate; no runtime behavior changed.
  "2026-07-26T15:08:27.500Z",codex,"Final CodeRabbit review hardening: indexed relevance candidates for linear lookup, skipped full-corpus pre-ranking without --max-items, labeled explain ranks as emitted-pack-relative, refreshed max-items docs, and documented the test's intentional non-recording parity call. The suggested malformed-settings fallback was not applied because canonical SDK list runs first and already rejects unreadable settings; hiding only the second read would not preserve pack availability."
  "2026-07-26T15:08:27.500Z",codex,"Supersedes the 2026-07-26T11:59:50.739Z intermediate parity note: the final SDK list call intentionally omits noTruncate to match the original shell command's default truncation semantics. The earlier scoreContextCandidates/evaluateContextRanking names were implementation-plan terminology; shipped code uses rankContextItems/createSdkPacker and buildContextExplain/scoreContextItems."
